WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.370
There are people in Hollywood called script
supervisors whose job is to make sure that

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:08.050
there aren't any silly or stupid continuity
mistakes in their movie.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:09.770
And often, they totally fail.

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:13.820
So don't worry if you never picked up on these
cinematic goofs, because here are some big

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.780
movie mistakes that everyone failed to notice.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.030
Terminator 3 plane switch

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:23.110
When John and Catherine decide to make an
airborne getaway, they head to a blue and

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:25.260
white Cessna parked in the hangar.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:30.070
As they enter the plane, the identifying numbers
on the side of the plane read "N3035C."

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:35.481
A subsequent shot of the plane flying over
the arid landscape shows that the plane number

00:00:35.481 --> 00:00:37.410
now is "N3973F."

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:43.140
Finally, when they land the plane, the number
switches one more time—back to the original

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.440
"N3035C."

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.590
Die Another Day's vanishing scar

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:53.050
In this James Bond adventure, Bond-girl Jinx
gets into a sabre fight with Miranda Frost.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:57.900
At one point during the fight, Jinx takes
a nasty slash to her midsection—splitting

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:01.100
her shirt open and leaving a bleeding shallow
wound.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:06.040
Later, 007 and Jinx are reveling in the hoard
of diamonds, and he pours a handful across

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:09.970
her stomach—which is completely unblemished
by any scratches or wounds.

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:10.970
Oops!

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.770
Harry Potter and the magic shirt

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:17.180
In Harry Potter and the Order of the Phoenix,
Harry has a bad dream after an argument with

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:19.360
Seamus in the Gryffindor common room.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.770
During that dream, Harry is shown thrashing
around in a light blue crew-neck t-shirt.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:27.590
When he wakes up, he sits up and is wearing
a dark blue button-up Henley shirt.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:32.130
That Henley actually comes from a later dream
sequence in the film, when Harry is dreaming

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:35.130
about Arthur Weasley in the Department of
Mysteries.

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:37.869
Rocky Horror Picture Show's vanishing jewelry

00:01:37.869 --> 00:01:42.420
Eddie has the words "LOVE" and "HATE" tattooed
on his knuckles in Rocky Horror Picture Show,

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:47.200
and his left hand is accessorized with several
rings—including an Iron Cross pinky ring.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.150
Eagle-eyed Rocky Horror fans may notice that
the ring disappears while Eddie plays saxophone,

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:54.900
only to reappear later with no explanation.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.369
Even the rings aren't what they appear in
Rocky Horror!

00:01:57.369 --> 00:01:59.729
Terminator 2's magic windshield

00:01:59.729 --> 00:02:05.040
In a pivotal scene, the T-1000 commandeers
a helicopter, literally headbutting through

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.950
the windshield to gain entry and take control.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:10.189
This leaves a gaping hole in the shattered
glass.

00:02:10.189 --> 00:02:14.579
But later in a zoomed-out shot of the helicopter
pursuing Sarah Connor and the Terminator on

00:02:14.579 --> 00:02:17.230
a highway, the windshield is magically fixed.

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:21.930
The magic helicopter gets even crazier after
it somehow explodes, then somehow immediately

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.629
repairs itself and then explodes again.

00:02:24.629 --> 00:02:26.469
Lord of the Wrists

00:02:26.469 --> 00:02:31.040
Merry and Pippin are taken captive by the
Uruk-hai in The Lord of the Rings: The Two

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.040
Towers.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:35.180
“Looks like meat is back on our menu, boys!”

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:40.010
But they manage to escape during a middle-of-the-night
raid by the horselords of Rohan.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:43.159
The hobbits crawl away from the battle, hindered
by their bound hands.

00:02:43.159 --> 00:02:47.749
At one point, however, Pippin is nearly trampled
by a horse, and he rolls on his back and flails

00:02:47.749 --> 00:02:50.150
his suddenly-untied hands around in fear.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:54.129
After the danger of getting stomped underfoot
has passed, he resumes crawling away with

00:02:54.129 --> 00:02:58.689
hands tied again, and he and Merry use a blade
to cut through their bonds.

00:02:58.689 --> 00:02:59.689
Gladiator tank

00:02:59.689 --> 00:03:04.639
During one of Gladiator's big fight sequences,
three different chariots end up flipping over.

00:03:04.639 --> 00:03:08.799
Pay close attention to the third chariot as
it lurches sideways and crashes—you can

00:03:08.799 --> 00:03:13.970
clearly see a tank of some sort of compressed
gas used in the stunt just hanging out, strapped

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:15.829
to the bottom of the chariot.

00:03:15.829 --> 00:03:16.820
“Are you not entertained?

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.280
“Are you not entertained?!"

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:21.340
Alien hoodie

00:03:21.349 --> 00:03:25.689
Fans of the original Alien may have spotted
one glaring continuity error with the film's

00:03:25.689 --> 00:03:26.689
wardrobe.

00:03:26.689 --> 00:03:30.379
When the crew is exploring the boneship, Kane
is shown wearing a close-fitting cloth hood

00:03:30.379 --> 00:03:31.760
under his space helmet.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:35.540
He's attacked by a facehugger, and when they
cut his helmet off, the hood is nowhere to

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:36.540
be seen.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:37.840
Maybe the alien ate it?

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:41.420
“Oh no!

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:43.720
Not again!”

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.099
Wizard of Oz slipper switch

00:03:47.099 --> 00:03:51.159
Even the most famous props in movie history
were involved in an on-screen screw-up.

00:03:51.159 --> 00:03:56.219
Yes, Dorothy's ruby slippers do the disappearing
act during a sequence when she and Scarecrow

00:03:56.219 --> 00:03:57.989
get attacked by an apple tree.

00:03:57.989 --> 00:04:02.889
Instead, she's wearing a pair of decidedly
non-magical black and tan lace-up saddle shoes.

00:04:02.889 --> 00:04:04.349
There's no place like Payless!

00:04:04.349 --> 00:04:05.709
Thanks for watching!

00:04:05.709 --> 00:04:08.760
